# Windows reserved-name artifacts (`nul` is the null device on Windows;
# some PowerShell commands accidentally create a literal file called
# `nul` when `> nul` is used as a redirect). The file can't be
# deleted by name from a normal PowerShell — open File Explorer and
# delete it manually, or run from an elevated cmd:
#   del \\.\e:\code\autobot\autobot-frontend\nul
